{"name":"Azure Mist","hex":"#f0fff1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"azure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The clear blue colour of the sky; also, a pigment or dye of this colour.","A blue colour on a coat of arms, represented in engraving by horizontal parallel lines."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sky blue; resembling the clear blue colour of the unclouded sky.","Cloudless."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/azure"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of cyan","blocks":[{"text":"The color cyan, a color between green and blue, has notable tints and shades. It is one of the subtractive primary colors, along with magenta and yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Color_icon_cyan.svg/330px-Color_icon_cyan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_cyan","wikidata":"Q7915816"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.